      "title": "FHIR core definitions",
      "description": "The FHIR core specification's StructureDefinitions for each STABLE release, one graph per release keyed by canonical URL (http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/<id>): R4 from `hl7.fhir.r4.core#4.0.1`, R4B from `hl7.fhir.r4b.core#4.3.0`, R5 from `hl7.fhir.r5.core#5.0.0`, each pinned in `pins.json` by its packages.fhir.org URL, sha1 and sha512. `<release>/manifest.json` lists every resource, complex and primitive type and root type (Base in R5; Element, BackboneElement, DomainResource, Resource) with its kind, base and the sha256 of its bytes; constraint profiles, extension definitions and logical models are left out and counted. The bodies are the package's own files, written beside the manifest by `fhir-core.ts materialise` and not committed (12 MB); `fhir-core.ts check` holds them to the manifests and `resolve` answers which file a canonical is kept in. A release whose package could not be read is `unread` with the reason, never an empty graph (owner, 2026-11-14).",
      "fileCount": 0,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/fhir-harness/directory/fhir-core-definitions"
